title: '[pallet-session] fix orphaned consumer reference and locked deposit when keys
  are purged by a different account'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Fixes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/270

    `set_keys` places a key deposit and consumer reference on the dispatching account, but the keys
    are stored against its `ValidatorId`. `purge_keys` reversed both against the dispatching
    account, so after a stash/controller change purging from the new controller freed them from the
    wrong account, leaving the original one with an unremovable consumer reference and locked
    deposit.

    Fixed by recording the placing account per `ValidatorId` (new `KeyRegistrant` map) and always
    reversing the deposit and consumer reference against it, so either the stash or controller may
    purge. The map starts empty and needs no migration; pre-existing keys fall back to the previous
    behaviour.
crates:
- name: pallet-session
  bump: minor
